{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/948269-2e-promethean-supplements","id":948269,"title":"2e Promethean Supplements","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-10T19:26:36-07:00","id":948269,"title":"2e Promethean Supplements","content":"What would you like to see? <br /> <br /> Personally, I'd love to see a supplement that relates the created to real-world alchemical texts, both the very occult and the very practical, this-is-how-you-make-imitation-silver kind. Given that this ranges from Egypt papyri and concepts of hidden gods, to Aristotle, to Gnosticism, to the Emerald Tablet to Issac Newton, I feel like that's real fertile and interesting ground to cover.<br /> <br /> And Night Horrors. (And obviously more Dark Eras, but given the glut in the Companion, I'll hold off on requesting those until after I see the upcoming ones)<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T20:52:25-07:00","id":948322,"title":"","content":"Lineages Books! that go really deep into LineagesHistorys, mindsets and notorious members,with new bestowements and transmutations to boot.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T20:52:33-07:00","id":948323,"title":"","content":"Frankly, I wouldn't mind 2e counterparts to the original line of supplements, albeit with some reorganization. <br /> <br /> <b>Pandora's Book</b>: not just Centimani, Pandorans, <i>qashmallim</i>, and Firestorms; but also Zeka, more nuanced and detailed alchemists, homunculi, beast-men from the Isle of Dr. Moreau, etc. The <b>Night Horrors</b> book. <br /> <br /> <b>Strange Alchemies</b>: optional rules for Constructed Prometheans; more Bestowments and an expanded system for Bestowments (and Boons?) designed to allow for more fine-tuning of the Lineages and to provide for an easier hook for adding new powers to the game; more Roles per Refinement; more Alembics per Transmutation; a closer look at Athanors; more Azothic Items. The Player's Guide. <br /> <br /> <b>Magnum Opus</b>: the <b>World of Darkness: Mirrors</b> of the <b>Promethean</b> line, with rules variants and setting shards. The Chronicler's Guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T22:40:21-07:00","id":948383,"title":"","content":"A book on the level of the Demon Storyteller's Guide of Vampire's 1e Danse Macabre would be a godsend. Promethean is one of the most demanding games for a Storyteller, so a tome of advice aimed specifically at them and stuffed with optional rules and shards is much more pressing in my eyes than, say, a player's guide with some new Bestowments.<br /> <br /> Other than that, a book at least partly focused on new, alternate, and historical Lineages (with an extensive guide to building your own) would be stellar. We know Fire had one Lineage before the Wretched in the Prophets, and while the Osirans and Galateid seem to span back into distant history, I'm sure the elements, humours, and Divine Fire don't limit themselves to so few avenues of exprssion. This would also be an awesome chance to bring back those 1e ideas of Lineages with Vitae as a humour or an Awakened demiurge, but as full Lineages rather than one-off miracles. Promethean is a game about being a unique experiment, so breaking away from a monolithic &quot;these are the five main Lineages&quot; is only a good thing in my eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T23:13:14-07:00","id":948397,"title":"","content":"I actually wonder if it'd be possible to support a book specifically about Refinements. Come up with some more Roles for each, flesh them all out with light fiction? Dunno. Seems light.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T23:47:39-07:00","id":948408,"title":"","content":"Elan Vital must be a name.<br /> <br /> I would not object to it being the name for an alchemist and demiurge book, though I imagine better can be done.<br /> <br /> Imposter Syndrome would be a cool Players Guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T04:18:52-07:00","id":948503,"title":"","content":"I don't know about whole books, but I have thoughts on what content I'd like.<br /> <br /> Further detail given to Alchemists.<br /> Possibly more Refinements, Roles and Transmutations.<br /> Some new Lineages and Bestowments, alongside the return of the Zeka.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, I don't know. Promethean already feels like a very complete game. A Storyteller/Player's Guide and Lineage Books do seem like great ideas, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T07:16:09-07:00","id":948582,"title":"","content":"<b>Capax Infiniti:</b> A book about the successes and excesses of science from all points of view. Mortals, Alchemists, Prometheans, crossover material with Mages, the Ordo Dracul, etc... Rules for alchemical potions, alliances between Prometheans and Alchemists, probably playable Alchemists in here too.<br /> <br /> <b>Ad Fontes:</b> A look back at Promethean's history and origins. Old Prometheans, forgotten lineages, forgotten alchemical prowesses, an in-depth explanation of the Azothic Memory, Pilgrim Altars left around the globe.<br /> <br /> <b>Mala Fide:</b> A book about those who turn to the dark forces of the Flux knowingly. A reimagining of Pandora's Book, in a way, it explores Centimani, Alchemists who turned to their trade due to Disquiet and their hate of the Promethean condition, Lilithims and the various reasons and applications of the entropic force of Flux.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T07:28:18-07:00","id":948590,"title":"","content":"More fiction! Stories showing the pilgrimage!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T07:36:48-07:00","id":948598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <stro